@jogiches
title: The Zentrale
new-page: true
on-arrival: {!
if (!Q.jogiches_alive) {
    Q.luxemburgist_satisfaction -= 5;
    Q.spd_relation -= 5;
}
if (Q.luxemburg_alive) {
    Q.party_chair = 'Rosa Luxemburg';
    Q.levi_chair = 0;
} else if (Q.jogiches_alive) {
    Q.party_chair = 'Leo Jogiches';
    Q.levi_chair = 0;
} else {
    Q.party_chair = 'Paul Levi';
    Q.levi_chair = 1;
}
!}

= The Zentrale

[? if jogiches_alive = 0 : On 10 March Leo Jogiches is arrested in his flat in Neukölln and taken to the remand prison in Moabit. That evening a police sergeant, Ernst Tamschick, shoots him in the back in a corridor, "while trying to escape". The man who built the Spartacus League in secret through four years of war is dead. ?][? if jogiches_alive = 1 : The police come to Jogiches' flat in Neukölln on 10 March and find it empty. He has learned the trade of hiding in the Tsar's empire, and he has not forgotten it. ?]

[? if levi_chair = 1 : The leadership passes to **Paul Levi**, a thirty-five-year-old Frankfurt lawyer, Luxemburg's defender in court and her closest political friend. He is cool, cultivated and impatient with fools, and the Left Radicals detest him. He means to turn a sect of rebels into a party that can win the working class. ?][? if levi_chair = 0 and luxemburg_alive = 1 : **Rosa Luxemburg** still leads the Zentrale from hiding, with Paul Levi as her right hand. ?][? if levi_chair = 0 and luxemburg_alive = 0 : **Leo Jogiches** still holds the Zentrale together, with Paul Levi as his right hand. ?]

The party goes underground. It is smaller in Berlin than in January, and growing everywhere else.
